1. Definitions

   "Software" means Promulga: the source code, Docker images, templates and
   documentation in this repository, and any part or modified version of them.

   "Editor" means an active user account of an installation that can take part
   in the document workflow: contributor (owner, reviewer, approver), manager or
   administrator. Readers of a portal open without sign-in have no account and
   are not Editors.

   "Organisation" means a legal entity together with the entities it controls,
   is controlled by, or is under common control with.

2. Free use

   You may use, copy, modify and run the Software, at no cost, for:

   a) any non-commercial purpose (personal use, education, research, non-profit
      organisations), and
   b) the internal operations of an Organisation, including a company or a
      public body, provided that the installations of that Organisation have in
      total no more than 20 Editors at any time.

   Readers of a public portal (without sign-in) are unlimited.

3. Conditions

   a) Keep this license and the copyright notice in every copy or substantial
      portion of the Software, and do not remove the attribution "Promulga, by
      Olivier Bouchez Data Consulting" from the user interface footer.
   b) If you distribute a modified version, state that you changed it and
      distribute it under this same license.

4. Uses that need a written permission

   The following uses require a separate, written agreement with the licensor
   (sales@promulga.com):

   a) more than 20 Editors in one Organisation;
   b) selling, renting or sublicensing the Software or a modified version;
   c) providing the Software to third parties as a hosted or managed service
      (SaaS), or operating it for clients;
   d) embedding the Software, or a substantial part of it, in a product or a
      service that is sold.

   Consulting, installation, configuration or training services around an
   installation owned and operated by the client itself, within the limits of
   section 2, do not need a permission.

